D3D12: the micromap prebuild query passes dummy non-zero buffer addresses.

DeviceD3D12::GetMicromapPrebuildInfo queries the size of an opacity micromap array from its usage
histogram alone and leaves InputBuffer and PerOmmDescs null, while every build passes real
addresses. The DXR spec allows the prebuild query to inspect whether a GPU address is null ("even
though the pointers are not dereferenced") and says "dummy non-zero values can be used just for the
purposes for the prebuild call" for entries the build fills in; the Agility debug layer refuses the
null ones at every micromap creation: "[1162] GetRaytracingAccelerationStructurePrebuildInfo:
pDesc->pOpacityMicromapArrayDesc->pOmmHistogram indicate 2 OMMs in total, so InputBuffer and
PerOmmDescs can't be null" (v191, Agility 1.620, RTX 4070 SUPER; main b90cfb57 has the same code).

This passes 256 for both (InputBuffer must be 128-byte aligned, PerOmmDescs 4-byte) with the build's
stride, sizeof(MicromapTriangle). Measured: no [1162] at micromap creation, and the micromaps,
bound, placed, cloned and compacted, still decide the ray query as before.

diff --git a/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp
index bcdcbd09..11d6e542 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp
@@ -1638,6 +1638,11 @@ void DeviceD3D12::GetMicromapPrebuildInfo(const MicromapDesc& micromapDesc, D3D1
     opacityMicromapArrayDesc.NumOmmHistogramEntries = micromapDesc.usageNum;
     opacityMicromapArrayDesc.pOmmHistogram = usages;
 
+    // Not dereferenced, but may be checked for null: dummy non-zero values stand for the build's buffers (DXR spec, "GetRaytracingAccelerationStructurePrebuildInfo")
+    opacityMicromapArrayDesc.InputBuffer = 256;
+    opacityMicromapArrayDesc.PerOmmDescs.StartAddress = 256;
+    opacityMicromapArrayDesc.PerOmmDescs.StrideInBytes = sizeof(MicromapTriangle);
+
     D3D12_BUILD_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_INPUTS accelerationStructureInputs = {};
     accelerationStructureInputs.Type = D3D12_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_TYPE_OPACITY_MICROMAP_ARRAY;
     accelerationStructureInputs.Flags = GetMicromapFlags(micromapDesc.flags);
